<title>UK: Belgacom sets 10 bln yen multi-currency 30-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Belgacom sets 10 bln yen multi-currency 30-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Yamaichi International and Sanwa International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BELGACOM N.V. VAN PUBLIEK RECHT</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON     **	  MATURITY    16.DEC.26</p>
<p> TYPE  MULTI-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  100.50    PAY DATE    16.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  50 BP     LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   DENOMS (M) 100	 SALE LIMITS ***</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> NOTES    **AT THE OPTION OF ISSUER THE COUPON IS PAYABLE EITHER</p>
<p>		IN AUSTRALIAN DOLLARS AT 6.07 PCT, MARKS AT 5.67 PCT</p>
<p>		OR U.S. DOLLARS AT 5.87 PCT.</p>
<p>	   ***US/UK/JAPAN/BELGIUM/GERMANY</p>
<p>		SENIOR, UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
